E["npc:hansel-heavyhands"] = {t="npc",n="Hansel Heavyhands",z="searinggorge",s="At Thorium Point, Hansel Heavyhands is given dangerous work below the outpost. The huge Dark Iron dwarf passes those jobs to travelers and offers a string of complaints.",h="At Thorium Point, Hansel Heavyhands is given dangerous work below the outpost.",sec={{t="A Giant Among Dwarves",b="At Thorium Point, Hansel Heavyhands towers over the other Dark Iron dwarves. His broad frame is nearly as tall and wide as an orc's. He seems made for the front line, yet avoids needless exertion. Instead, he stays in the Thorium Brotherhood's camp above the volcanic ash.",sp=0},{t="Master of Excuses",b="Taskmaster Scrange and Master Smith Burninate send Hansel after dangerous beasts in the slag pits. When told to clear Incendosaurs from the Cauldron, he pleads sore feet. Ordered to kill Greater Lava Spiders in the searing wastes, he claims the volcanic ridge is so cold that he has caught a miserable chill. Travelers willing to brave the magma flows can take the work instead.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Hansel Heavyhands?",a="Hansel Heavyhands serves with the Thorium Brotherhood at Thorium Point in the Searing Gorge. His enormous size draws notice, and he avoids dangerous fieldwork.",al={"who is hansel","hansel heavyhands lore","hansel dwarf"}},{q="Why is Hansel so much bigger than other dwarves?",a="No clear explanation is given for Hansel's size. The Dark Iron dwarf is abnormally large, with broad shoulders, thick limbs, and a stature approaching an orc's.",al={"why is hansel so big","huge dwarf searing gorge","orc sized dwarf"}},{q="What tasks does Hansel give to adventurers?",a="Hansel gives travelers work assigned by his superiors. He pays them to hunt Greater Lava Spiders across the Searing Gorge and Incendosaurs in the Cauldron.",al={"hansel heavyhands quests","what quests does hansel give"}},{q="Why doesn't Hansel do his own chores?",a="Hansel makes excuses when dangerous work comes his way. He blames sore feet to avoid Incendosaurs and claims the hot Searing Gorge has given him a cold when ordered to hunt lava spiders.",al={"why doesnt hansel fight","hansel excuses"}},{q="Is Hansel loyal to the Dark Iron emperor?",a="Hansel belongs to the Thorium Brotherhood, a renegade faction of Dark Iron dwarves that broke away from Emperor Dagran Thaurissan and Ragnaros. He is neutral toward Alliance and Horde travelers at Thorium Point.",al={"is hansel loyal to shadowforge","is hansel an enemy"}},{q="Where can Hansel Heavyhands be found?",a="Hansel Heavyhands can be found at Thorium Point, the rocky outpost on the northern ridge overlooking the Searing Gorge.",al={"hansel location","where is hansel"}}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a Bronzebeard or Wildhammer dwarf, you may marvel at Hansel's colossal build or wonder how a Dark Iron grew so large while avoiding hard work.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler, you can find local bounty work with the Thorium Brotherhood. It welcomes anyone with a strong arm despite the Alliance's clashes with Dark Iron loyalists.",["faction:Horde"]="As a Horde traveler, you may find Hansel's bulk reminiscent of an orc or tauren, while his reluctance to fight may surprise you."},kw={"cauldron","dark iron","hansel heavyhands","incendosaur","lava spider","searing gorge","thorium brotherhood","thorium point"},rel={"subzone:thorium-point","zone:searinggorge","subzone:cauldron","topic:dark-iron-dwarf","topic:dwarf","topic:alliance","topic:horde"},src={"Hansel Heavyhands"}}
E["npc:velarok"] = {t="npc",n="Velarok",z="searinggorge",s="Among the ash and slain dwarves in Searing Gorge, Velarok Windblade asks travelers to help him forge vengeance.",h="Among the ash and slain dwarves in Searing Gorge, Velarok Windblade asks travelers to help him forge...",sec={{t="A Son's Vengeance",b="Southeast of Thorium Point, Velarok Windblade camps in the wastes of Searing Gorge. Dark Iron dwarves lie dead around him, slain in the fight he says began with his father's murder. He asks travelers to gather what he needs to make the Torch of Retribution. The enchanted weapon is meant for the Dark Irons and Ragnaros's minions.",sp=0},{t="The Deceiver Unmasked",b="Velarok's slain father is a lie. Once the Torch of Retribution is assembled and energized, his human guise breaks. Beneath it stands Velarok the Deceiver, a cunning drake of the black dragonflight. He used mortals to weaken the Dark Iron dwarves for his brood's designs. Amused by the help they have given, Velarok spares them. His servant leaves them petty trinkets, and the drake flies toward Blackrock Mountain.",sp=2}},faq={{q="Who is Velarok?",a="Southeast of Thorium Point in Searing Gorge, Velarok Windblade appears to be a vengeful human swordsman. He seeks retribution against the Dark Iron clan for his father's death.",al={"who is velarok windblade","velarok identity","velarok lore"},sp=2},{q="Why is Velarok surrounded by dead dwarves?",a="Velarok says the Dark Iron dwarves around his camp were killed in the blood feud over his father's death.",al={"mutilated dark iron remains","dead dwarves near velarok","velarok camp bodies"},sp=2},{q="What is the Torch of Retribution?",a="The Torch of Retribution is an enchanted weapon made from rare materials gathered across Searing Gorge for vengeance. Velarok has his helpers collect the pieces, then combines and enchants them himself before binding the finished torch to the one who helped him.",al={"torch quest velarok","what is the torch of retribution"},sp=1},{q="Why does Velarok disguise himself as a human?",a="A human guise lets Velarok recruit Alliance and Horde adventurers without raising suspicion. Black dragons often take mortal forms to direct attacks against enemies such as Ragnaros's Dark Iron servants.",al={"why is velarok human","why deceive players","velarok the deceiver disguise"},sp=2},{q="Where does Velarok go after revealing himself?",a="After revealing his dragon form as Velarok the Deceiver, he flies toward Blackrock Mountain to rejoin his brood. His mortal servant gives trinkets to the adventurers who helped him.",al={"where did velarok fly","velarok ending","what happens to velarok"},sp=2},{q="Does Velarok attack when his disguise drops?",a="No. Velarok finds the adventurers' unwitting service amusing and satisfactory. He spares them, and his servant gives them minor trinkets.",al={"do i fight velarok","does velarok turn hostile"},sp=2}},ang={["race:Human"]="As a human, Velarok's tale of a murdered father and a son's vengeance appeals to ideals of filial duty and righteous retribution.",["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, the Dark Iron dwarves are enemies of Ironforge, so a stranger's vow of vengeance against them may find sympathy among Bronzebeards. Yet Searing Gorge holds cunning dangers beyond the Dark Irons."},kw={"searing gorge","thorium point","torch of retribution","velarok","velarok windblade"},rel={"zone:searinggorge","topic:black-dragonflight","subzone:blackrock-mountain","subzone:thorium-point"},src={"Velarok"}}
E["quest:3181"] = {t="quest",n="The Horn of the Beast",z="searinggorge",s="In Searing Gorge, Margol the Rager's horn bears a broken axe head.",h="In Searing Gorge, Margol the Rager's horn bears a broken axe head.",sec={{t="A Shattered Clue",b="Margol the Rager's horn is scratched and cracked. A broken axe head is lodged in its rough surface, and Mountaineer Pebblebitty's name marks the metal. When you try to free it, the axe head shatters into a million pieces.",sp=0},{t="The Gate",b="Stonewrought Pass runs between Loch Modan and Searing Gorge. The horn begins the chain that opens the gate, and you are to take it to Mountaineer Pebblebitty. Pebblebitty is not willing to open the gate.",sp=0},{t="At the Gate",b="Mountaineer Pebblebitty calls the horn an obvious fake. Pebblebitty has faced Margol and says her horn is far bigger than yours, at least eight times its size. Pebblebitty says yours probably came from a stormsnout in the Barrens.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where does this horn come from?",a="Margol the Rager's horn comes from Searing Gorge.",al={"where do i find the horn","margol the rager location","who drops the horn"}},{q="Who is Mountaineer Pebblebitty?",a="Mountaineer Pebblebitty is the mountaineer you are to take the horn to. Pebblebitty is unwilling to open the gate.",al={"pebblebitty","who is pebblebitty","mountaineer pebblebitty"}},{q="What happens to the axe head in the horn?",a="The axe head bears Mountaineer Pebblebitty's name. When you try to free it, it shatters into a million pieces.",al={"why was pebblebitty axe in the horn","axe head inscription"}},{q="What does the horn lead to?",a="The horn begins the chain that opens Stonewrought Pass between Loch Modan and Searing Gorge.",al={"stonewrought pass","what is the key to searing gorge"},sp=1}},kw={"gigantic horn","loch modan","margol the rager","pebblebitty","searing gorge","stonewrought pass"},rel={"subzone:stonewrought-pass","zone:searinggorge","zone:lochmodan"},m={start="Margol's Gigantic Horn",["end"]="Mountaineer Pebblebitty",level="43",faction="Alliance",id=3181},src={"The Horn of the Beast"}}
E["quest:3367"] = {t="quest",n="Suntara Stones",z="searinggorge",s="In Searing Gorge, Dorius Stonetender lies badly hurt and asks you to help him reach Ironforge.",h="In Searing Gorge, Dorius Stonetender lies badly hurt and asks you to help him reach Ironforge.",sec={{t="A Plea for Help",b="Dorius Stonetender groans with pain. He feels light-headed as the world spins around him, and he is bleeding inside. He longs to return to Ironforge. So he asks you to help him make the journey.",sp=0},{t="The Road to the Pass",b="The road ends just short of Stonewrought Pass. There, Dorius is shot and dies. A letter he carried falls to the ground, singed.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Dorius Stonetender?",a="Dorius Stonetender is badly injured in Searing Gorge and needs help reaching Ironforge.",al={"who is dorius","dorius stonetender","injured dwarf searing gorge"}},{q="Where is Dorius trying to go?",a="Dorius is trying to return to Ironforge.",al={"dorius destination","where does dorius go","dorius escort location"}},{q="What condition is Dorius in?",a="Dorius is badly injured, light-headed, and bleeding inside. The world spins around him.",al={"dorius condition","is dorius hurt","why does dorius need help"}}},kw={"dorius stonetender","ironforge","searing gorge","singed letter","stonewrought pass","suntara stones"},rel={"zone:searinggorge","subzone:stonewrought-pass","zone:ironforge"},m={start="Dorius Stonetender",["end"]=":Singed Letter",level="46",faction="Alliance",id=3367},src={"Suntara Stones"}}
E["quest:3368"] = {t="quest",n="Suntara Stones",z="searinggorge",s="At the Suntara Stones, Dorius's letter tells of a team enslaved by the Dark Irons. The stones are real and held by the Dark Irons. Their leader, Lathoric the Black, uses the stones' power to enslave Dorius's excavation team. You carry the letter to his brother Thorius at Ironforge's Hall of Explorers.",h="At the Suntara Stones, Dorius's letter tells of a team enslaved by the Dark Irons.",sec={{t="The Dead Man's Letter",b="Dorius's letter tells his brother he is gone if the message is being read. The Suntara Stones are real, and the Dark Irons hold them. Their leader, Lathoric the Black, uses their power to enslave Dorius's excavation team. The team was taken to the cauldron, where their minds are twisted as they toil day and night to finish something called Obsidion. Dorius begs his brother to help them. He calls it his final wish and asks that those who bring the letter be thanked.",sp=0},{t="Thorius Hears the News",b="Curator Thorius sobs when Dorius's letter arrives. Then he dries his face and swears by the Light that Dorius will have his wish.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who wrote the singed letter?",a="Dorius wrote the singed letter to his brother, to be read after his death.",al={"who wrote the letter","author of singed letter","dorius letter"}},{q="Where does Thorius reside?",a="Curator Thorius resides in Ironforge's Hall of Explorers.",al={"where is thorius","curator thorius location","thorius hall of explorers"}},{q="What happened to Dorius's excavation team?",a="The letter says Lathoric the Black and the Dark Irons use the stones' power to enslave Dorius's excavation team. They took the team to the cauldron.",al={"what happened to the dig team","dorius excavation team","enslaved miners cauldron"}},{q="What is the enslaved team working on?",a="The letter says the team's minds are twisted as they toil day and night on something called Obsidion.",al={"what is obsidion","cauldron excavation project","dark iron project obsidion"}},{q="Who is Lathoric the Black?",a="The letter names Lathoric the Black as the leader of the Dark Irons. They hold the Suntara Stones and use their power to enslave Dorius's team.",al={"who is lathoric","lathoric the black","dark iron leader searing gorge"}},{q="How does this follow the earlier Suntara Stones?",a="The first Suntara Stones tells how Dorius was shot and the letter fell from him. You carry the letter to Ironforge.",al={"previous suntara stones quest","suntara stones chain"}}},kw={"cauldron","dorius","hall of explorers","ironforge","lathoric the black","obsidion","searing gorge","singed letter","suntara stones","thorius"},rel={"quest:3367","zone:ironforge","subzone:hall-of-explorers","subzone:cauldron","zone:searinggorge"},m={start=":Singed Letter",["end"]="Curator Thorius",level="48",faction="Alliance",id=3368},src={"Suntara Stones (2)"}}
E["quest:3372"] = {t="quest",n="Release Them",z="searinggorge",s="In Searing Gorge, a dying archaeologist begs you to free those still laboring under Suntara's power. Their bodies have failed, and the relic guarded by Twilight's Hammer must be placed on Suntara's altar.",h="In Searing Gorge, a dying archaeologist begs you to free those still laboring under Suntara's power.",sec={{t="A Dying Plea",b="A dying archaeologist asks you to release those still at their labor, then collapses. Their bodies have given out, yet Suntara's power drives them on. The archaeologist says Suntara's altar is the key.",sp=0},{t="The Altar of Suntara",b="Northwest of the cave, in the hills above it, Twilight's Hammer Idolaters guard the Mysterious Artifact. Take the relic from them and carry it to the Slag Pit. There, set it upon Suntara's altar.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who asks for help with Release Them?",a="A dying archaeologist in Searing Gorge asks for help, then collapses.",al={"quest giver","who gives release them","dying archaeologist"}},{q="Where is the mysterious artifact located?",a="Twilight's Hammer Idolaters guard the Mysterious Artifact in the northwest quadrant of Searing Gorge, in the hills above the cave.",al={"mysterious artifact location","where is the relic","twilight's hammer idolaters"}},{q="Where must the artifact be delivered?",a="Carry the artifact to the Slag Pit and set it on Suntara's altar.",al={"altar of suntara location","where is the altar","where do i take the artifact"}},{q="Why are the victims unable to rest?",a="The archaeologist says Suntara's power drives the victims to keep at their labor, though their bodies have given out.",al={"why release them","what is happening to them","suntara power"}}},kw={"altar of suntara","dying archaeologist","mysterious artifact","release them","searing gorge","slag pit","twilight's hammer"},rel={"subzone:slag-pit","topic:twilight-s-hammer","zone:searinggorge"},m={start="Dying Archaeologist",["end"]="Altar of Suntara",level="46",faction="Alliance",id=3372},src={"Release Them"}}
E["quest:3377"] = {t="quest",n="Prayer to Elune",z="searinggorge",s="In Searing Gorge, Zamael Lunthistle waits in a cage and asks for your help. Many years have passed since anyone visited him, and first he asks you to hear his tale.",h="In Searing Gorge, Zamael Lunthistle waits in a cage and asks for your help.",sec={{t="A Spirit in a Cage",b="Zamael Lunthistle greets you with praise to Elune. Many years have passed since anyone came to visit him. Now he asks for your help. First, hear his tale.",sp=0},{t="Zamael's Tale",b="As a young night elf from Darkshore, Zamael fell under the Twilight's Hammer's influence and turned from Elune. Then a vision from Elune woke him from his malaise as a follower of the old gods. In repentance, he carved his sorrow into a tablet of pure gold as a prayer to Elune.\n\nThe Twilight's Hammer found the tablet and branded him a blasphemer. They had him executed before his prayer was finished. Now Zamael's spirit is bound to the world and held in a cage as a warning to those who would betray the Twilight's Hammer's faith. He has accepted his fate, but the prayer must still be found.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Zamael Lunthistle?",a="Zamael Lunthistle is a spirit held in a cage in Searing Gorge. He asks you to hear his tale.",al={"who is zamael","zamael lunthistle lore","who is the ghost in the cage"}},{q="What does Zamael ask of you?",a="Zamael asks for your help. First, he asks you to hear his tale.",al={"what does zamael want","zamael request"}},{q="What comes after hearing Zamael's tale?",a="After hearing Zamael's tale, you can hear its second part from him.",al={"next step prayer to elune","prayer to elune chain"}}},kw={"darkshore","elune","lunthistle","prayer","repentance","searing gorge","tablet","twilight's hammer","zamael"},rel={"topic:twilight-s-hammer","topic:elune","topic:night-elf","topic:old-god","zone:darkshore","zone:searinggorge"},m={start="Zamael Lunthistle",["end"]="Zamael Lunthistle",level="50",faction="Alliance",id=3377},src={"Prayer to Elune (Classic)"}}
E["quest:3378"] = {t="quest",n="Prayer to Elune",z="searinggorge",s="At Zamael Lunthistle's request, you seek a prayer to Elune lost among the idol worshippers. Engraved on a golden tablet, it is meant for Astarii Starseeker in Darnassus.",h="At Zamael Lunthistle's request, you seek a prayer to Elune lost among the idol worshippers.",sec={{t="The Lost Prayer",b="Zamael Lunthistle's faith has awakened again. Yet he says that means little after the harm he has done to the world and its people. He expects no absolution. He asks only for his prayer to be heard, so you seek the golden tablet from the idol worshippers and carry it to Astarii Starseeker in Darnassus.",sp=0},{t="At the Temple of the Moon",b="At the Temple of the Moon, Astarii Starseeker tells you that Elune smiles upon you this evening. By your hand, a lost soul has returned to her. Astarii gives you thanks.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Zamael Lunthistle?",a="Zamael Lunthistle asks you to find his prayer to Elune. His faith has returned, though he has done countless acts of harm against the world.",al={"zamael lunthistle lore","who gives prayer to elune","zamael"}},{q="What is the prayer inscribed on?",a="Zamael's prayer is engraved on a golden tablet. He believes one of the idol worshippers carries it.",al={"prayer to elune item","golden tablet","what is the prayer"}},{q="To whom should the prayer be delivered?",a="Carry the prayer to Astarii Starseeker at the Temple of the Moon in Darnassus.",al={"who receives prayer to elune","astarii starseeker","where do i bring the prayer"}},{q="Does Zamael expect forgiveness for his past?",a="No. Zamael expects no absolution for his past, but asks that his prayer be heard.",al={"does zamael want forgiveness","zamael absolution"}}},kw={"astarii starseeker","darnassus","golden tablet","prayer to elune","searing gorge","temple of the moon","zamael lunthistle"},rel={"quest:3377","subzone:temple-of-the-moon","zone:darnassus","topic:elune","zone:searinggorge"},m={start="Zamael Lunthistle",["end"]="Astarii Starseeker",level="50",faction="Alliance",id=3378},src={"Prayer to Elune (2)"}}
E["quest:3441"] = {t="quest",n="Divine Retribution",z="searinggorge",s="In Searing Gorge, Kalaran Windblade tells you how his father died and why he seeks vengeance. Stormwind would not hear his plea, so he turns to a brave adventurer.",h="In Searing Gorge, Kalaran Windblade tells you how his father died and why he seeks vengeance.",sec={{t="A Father Slain",b="Kalaran says the filth in the cauldron killed his father. He pleaded with the Stormwind magistrate, but no one answered. He says Stormwind would rather deny this part of the world exists than send soldiers to see justice done.",sp=0},{t="A Call for Vengeance",b="Kalaran wants vengeance. Only a lumbering oaf of a squire stands with him, while the Dark Iron dwarves and Ragnaros's beasts could crush him alone. So he trusts a brave adventurer to face the cauldron's denizens. For anyone who helps, he promises riches beyond all dreams.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Kalaran Windblade?",a="Kalaran Windblade is a man in Searing Gorge whose father was slain. His squire stands with him as he seeks vengeance.",al={"who is kalaran","kalaran story","kalaran lore"}},{q="Why is Kalaran seeking retribution?",a="Kalaran blames the filth in the cauldron for killing his father, and seeks vengeance.",al={"why divine retribution","kalaran revenge","what happened to kalaran father"}},{q="Why didn't Stormwind help Kalaran?",a="Kalaran says the Stormwind magistrate ignored his pleas. He believes Stormwind would rather deny this part of the world exists than send soldiers to see justice done.",al={"stormwind refusal","why wont stormwind help","stormwind magistrate"}},{q="What threats does Kalaran mention?",a="Kalaran names the Dark Iron dwarves and Ragnaros's beasts as threats that could overwhelm him alone.",al={"who is in the cauldron","cauldron enemies","kalaran enemies"}},{q="What does Kalaran promise in exchange for help?",a="Kalaran promises riches beyond all dreams to a brave adventurer who helps him.",al={"kalaran offer","what does kalaran offer"}}},kw={"cauldron","dark iron","kalaran windblade","ragnaros","retribution","stormwind","vengeance","windblade"},rel={"subzone:cauldron","topic:stormwind-kingdom","zone:searinggorge"},m={start="Kalaran Windblade",["end"]="Kalaran Windblade",level="48",id=3441},src={"Divine Retribution"}}
E["quest:3442"] = {t="quest",n="The Flawless Flame",z="searinggorge",s="In Searing Gorge, Kalaran Windblade prepares to strike where it will hurt most. He means to burn the four sentry towers, opening the way for an offensive before anyone can react. First, he needs a torch of flawless flame.",h="In Searing Gorge, Kalaran Windblade prepares to strike where it will hurt most.",sec={{t="Preparing the Torch",b="After Divine Retribution, Kalaran Windblade lays out his plan. He means to burn the four sentry towers so an offensive can begin before anyone has time to react.\n\nFor that, he needs the right tool and the materials to make it. Bring Kalaran four hearts of flame and four globes of golem oil, and he will craft the torch of flawless flame. He points you toward the golems and elementals of these lands.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of collecting these materials?",a="Kalaran Windblade needs four hearts of flame and four globes of golem oil to make a torch that will set the four sentry towers ablaze.",al={"why collect flame and oil","purpose of flawless flame","torch of flawless flame reason"}},{q="Where do you find the required components?",a="Kalaran points you toward the golems and elementals of Searing Gorge.",al={"where to find golem oil","where to find heart of flame","flawless flame materials location"}},{q="What comes before this step?",a="This follows Divine Retribution, where you heard Kalaran Windblade's tale.",al={"flawless flame prerequisite","previous quest flawless flame"}},{q="Why burn the sentry towers?",a="Kalaran says the four sentry towers are where a blow will do the most harm. Once they burn, an offensive can begin before anyone has time to react.",al={"why sentry towers","sentry tower plan"}}},kw={"golem oil","heart of flame","kalaran windblade","searing gorge","sentry towers","torch of flawless flame"},rel={"quest:3441","zone:searinggorge"},m={start="Kalaran Windblade",["end"]="Kalaran Windblade",level="48",id=3442},src={"The Flawless Flame"}}
E["quest:3443"] = {t="quest",n="Forging the Shaft",z="searinggorge",s="After The Flawless Flame, Kalaran Windblade needs a shaft to hold its fire. Eight thorium plated daggers from the cauldron can be reforged into one.",h="After The Flawless Flame, Kalaran Windblade needs a shaft to hold its fire.",sec={{t="Enchanted Alloy",b="Kalaran Windblade needs a shaft and a casing to hold the flawless flame. In the cauldron, Dark Iron slavers and taskmasters wield enchanted thorium, a sturdy metal. Kalaran can break down eight of their daggers and reforge the alloy into a shaft.",sp=0},{t="A Sharp Tongue",b="When you bring the daggers, Kalaran offers jeering instead of thanks. He calls you an exceptional laborer, then asks if you have considered another vocation. Perhaps detective, junk collector, or one of those silly gnomes who comb Azeroth’s beaches with metal-detecting contraptions, hunting lost treasure.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why does Kalaran need thorium plated daggers?",a="Kalaran Windblade can break down the daggers’ alloy and reforge it into a shaft to help hold the flawless flame.",al={"why daggers","thorium plated daggers purpose","why thorium daggers"}},{q="Who carries the required daggers?",a="Dark Iron slavers and taskmasters in the cauldron wield weapons of enchanted thorium.",al={"who drops the daggers","where are the daggers","who has thorium daggers"}},{q="Where does this step fit into the chain?",a="It follows The Flawless Flame, when you gathered materials for the torch of flawless flame.",al={"what quest comes before forging the shaft","quest chain position"}},{q="How many daggers are required?",a="Kalaran asks you to bring eight thorium plated daggers.",al={"how many daggers","dagger count","how many thorium daggers"}}},kw={"cauldron","dark iron slaver","dark iron taskmaster","flawless flame","kalaran windblade","searing gorge","thorium plated dagger"},rel={"quest:3442","subzone:cauldron","zone:searinggorge","topic:gnome"},m={start="Kalaran Windblade",["end"]="Kalaran Windblade",level="48",id=3443},src={"Forging the Shaft"}}
E["quest:3452"] = {t="quest",n="The Flame's Casing",z="searinggorge",s="Kalaran Windblade seeks the last piece for the torch. A large Twilight's Hammer encampment is rumored to lie in the mountains to the northwest, where its people honor their god with symbols and idols. He wants one Symbol of Ragnaros.",h="Kalaran Windblade seeks the last piece for the torch.",sec={{t="A Piece for the Casing",b="Kalaran Windblade says the torch needs one last piece. A large Twilight's Hammer encampment is rumored to lie in the mountains to the northwest, with symbols and idols honoring its god. Their enchantment may give the torch a magical casing. Kalaran asks you for one Symbol of Ragnaros, hoping to draw out its magic. Without a suitable source of arcane energy, the torch of retribution cannot be finished.",sp=0},{t="The Symbol Examined",b="The Symbol of Ragnaros gives off a foul magic, just the kind Kalaran needs for his work.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is needed to create the flame's casing?",a="Kalaran Windblade asks you for one Symbol of Ragnaros, hoping to draw out its magic for the casing.",al={"flames casing item","what does kalaran need","symbol needed"}},{q="Where is the Twilight's Hammer encampment?",a="A large Twilight's Hammer encampment is rumored to lie in the mountains to the northwest.",al={"twilights hammer location","where is the cult camp","northwest mountains cult"}},{q="Why does Kalaran want a Symbol of Ragnaros?",a="Twilight's Hammer symbols and idols may carry enough enchantment for a magical casing. Kalaran hopes to draw that magic from one Symbol of Ragnaros.",al={"why symbol of ragnaros","ragnaros symbol purpose","what does the symbol do"}},{q="What comes before this step in the chain?",a="This follows Forging the Shaft, when Kalaran asked for thorium plated daggers to reforge into a shaft.",al={"previous quest","what quest before flames casing"}}},kw={"flame's casing","kalaran windblade","searing gorge","symbol of ragnaros","torch of retribution","twilight's hammer"},rel={"quest:3443","topic:twilight-s-hammer","zone:searinggorge"},m={start="Kalaran Windblade",["end"]="Kalaran Windblade",level="50",id=3452},src={"The Flame's Casing"}}
E["quest:3453"] = {t="quest",n="The Torch of Retribution",z="searinggorge",s="At Kalaran Windblade's side, you wait while he joins the pieces and enchants The Torch of Retribution.",h="At Kalaran Windblade's side, you wait while he joins the pieces and enchants The Torch of Retribution.",sec={{t="Binding the Pieces",b="Kalaran Windblade needs time to join the pieces and enchant the torch. He channels magic as he works, so you wait and leave him undisturbed.",sp=0},{t="When the Wait Ends",b="After a while, the torch appears before Kalaran, and he says the work is done. One final matter remains for you to see to.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who crafts the torch?",a="Kalaran Windblade joins the pieces and enchants the torch. He channels magic to complete it.",al={"torch crafter","who makes the torch","kalaran windblade role"}},{q="What came right before this step?",a="The Flame's Casing came just before this. You found a Symbol of Ragnaros for Kalaran to make into the casing.",al={"previous quest","prerequisite","what did i just do"}},{q="Why must you not interrupt Kalaran?",a="Kalaran is channeling magic as he joins the pieces. He warns you not to interrupt him.",al={"do not interrupt","channeling process"}}},kw={"channeling","enchantment","kalaran windblade","searing gorge","torch of retribution"},rel={"quest:3452","zone:searinggorge"},m={start="Kalaran Windblade",["end"]="Kalaran Windblade",level="50",id=3453},src={"The Torch of Retribution"}}
E["quest:3454"] = {t="quest",n="The Torch of Retribution",z="searinggorge",s="Kalaran Windblade has finished the torch and asks you to claim it.",h="Kalaran Windblade has finished the torch and asks you to claim it.",sec={{t="Binding the Flame",b="Kalaran Windblade says the torch must be bound to its owner. He asks you to take it up yourself.",sp=0},{t="The Torch in Hand",b="Hatred and anger surge through you when you lift the torch in both hands.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who tells you to take the torch?",a="Kalaran Windblade tells you to take the torch so it can be bound to its owner.",al={"who gives the torch","torch quest giver","kalaran torch"}},{q="Why must you pick up the torch?",a="Kalaran says the torch must be bound to its owner, so he asks you to take it up.",al={"why pick up the torch","torch binding"}},{q="Where does this step fit into the chain?",a="This follows the earlier Torch of Retribution step, when you waited as Kalaran combined the pieces and enchanted them.",al={"torch quest chain","previous quest"}}},kw={"binding","kalaran windblade","searing gorge","torch of retribution"},rel={"quest:3453","zone:searinggorge"},m={start="Kalaran Windblade",["end"]=":Torch of Retribution",level="50",id=3454},src={"The Torch of Retribution (2)"}}
E["quest:3462"] = {t="quest",n="Squire Maltrake",z="searinggorge",s="With the Torch of Retribution in hand, Kalaran Windblade sends you to Squire Maltrake for instructions.",h="With the Torch of Retribution in hand, Kalaran Windblade sends you to Squire Maltrake for instructions.",sec={{t="A Word with the Envoy",b="Kalaran Windblade sends you to Squire Maltrake. The squire will explain how to use the Torch of Retribution.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who sends you to Squire Maltrake?",a="Kalaran Windblade sends you to Squire Maltrake and directs you to hear the instructions.",al={"who gives squire maltrake","squire maltrake questgiver","who starts squire maltrake"}},{q="What is Squire Maltrake's role?",a="Squire Maltrake will explain how to use the Torch of Retribution.",al={"what does squire maltrake do","who is maltrake","why talk to maltrake"}},{q="What comes before speaking to Squire Maltrake?",a="You receive the Torch of Retribution before speaking to Squire Maltrake.",al={"prerequisite squire maltrake","what quest comes before squire maltrake","previous quest maltrake"}}},kw={"envoy","kalaran windblade","searing gorge","squire maltrake","torch of retribution"},rel={"quest:3454","zone:searinggorge"},m={start="Kalaran Windblade",["end"]="Squire Maltrake",level="50",id=3462},src={"Squire Maltrake (quest)"}}
E["quest:3463"] = {t="quest",n="Set Them Ablaze!",z="searinggorge",s="In Searing Gorge, you carry Maltrake’s torch to the four sentry towers. Its flames cannot be subdued, and the towers cannot be destroyed. While they burn, guards and sentries abandon their posts, leaving the Dark Irons without their first line of defense.",h="In Searing Gorge, you carry Maltrake’s torch to the four sentry towers.",sec={{t="A Fire No Force Can Subdue",b="The Torch of Retribution burns beyond the power of any element or force to subdue. Maltrake sends you into each of the four sentry towers, North, South, East and West, to use it within the walls. Dark Iron lookouts keep watch there, so Maltrake warns you to beware.",sp=0},{t="After the Last Flame",b="When you return to Maltrake after the last tower burns, he cries out in triumph to his master. Velarok the Deceiver answers, revealing himself as a drake of the black dragonflight. His plan has worked perfectly, he gloats, because you would never have aided the Blackrock legion if they had simply asked.\n\nMaltrake wonders what to do with you, but Velarok silences him. You will live to watch the Blackrock legion invade the gorge. Velarok has Maltrake hand over trinkets, speaks of a molt, then flies toward the gorge.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who sends you to set the towers ablaze?",a="Squire Maltrake sends you to the towers and gives you the Torch of Retribution.",al={"who gives set them ablaze","set them ablaze quest giver","maltrake quest"}},{q="Which towers must be ignited?",a="Enter and ignite the four sentry towers: North, South, East and West.",al={"which towers","sentry tower locations","set them ablaze towers"}},{q="Why use the Torch of Retribution instead of tearing down the towers?",a="The towers cannot be destroyed. The Torch of Retribution keeps them burning for ages, and no element or force can subdue its flames.",al={"why torch","destroy sentry towers"}},{q="What was the previous step before this one?",a="You spoke with Squire Maltrake, who then gave you this undertaking.",al={"set them ablaze prerequisite","prior quest"}}},kw={"dark iron","searing gorge","sentry towers","set them ablaze","squire maltrake","torch of retribution"},rel={"quest:3462","quest:3481","zone:searinggorge","topic:black-dragonflight"},m={start="Squire Maltrake",["end"]="Squire Maltrake",level="52",id=3463},src={"Set Them Ablaze! (Classic)"}}
E["quest:3481"] = {t="quest",n="Trinkets...",z="searinggorge",s="After Set Them Ablaze!, you find the Hoard of the Black Dragonflight in Searing Gorge.",h="After Set Them Ablaze!, you find the Hoard of the Black Dragonflight in Searing Gorge.",sec={{t="A Locked Chest",b="The Hoard of the Black Dragonflight waits in Searing Gorge after the towers burn. The chest looks locked, and it is yours to open.",sp=0},{t="At Your Touch",b="The chest opens at your touch without a key. Inside lies a black dragonflight molt. Could there be cheese in there? The only way to know is to look.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the Hoard of the Black Dragonflight?",a="The Hoard of the Black Dragonflight is a chest in Searing Gorge that appears after Set Them Ablaze!. It looks locked.",al={"what is hoard of the black dragonflight","who owns the chest","trinkets chest location"}},{q="What comes before the chest?",a="Set Them Ablaze!, when you set fire to the towers of Searing Gorge.",al={"trinkets prerequisite","prior quest","what leads to trinkets"}},{q="What are you asked to do with the chest?",a="You are asked to open the chest. It looks locked, but opening it is all that is asked of you.",al={"is the chest locked","how to open the chest","what to do with the chest"}}},kw={"hoard of the black dragonflight","searing gorge","set them ablaze","trinkets"},rel={"quest:3463","zone:searinggorge","topic:black-dragonflight"},m={start="Hoard of the Black Dragonflight",["end"]="Hoard of the Black Dragonflight",level="50",id=3481},src={"Trinkets..."}}
E["quest:3566"] = {t="quest",n="Rise, Obsidion!",z="searinggorge",s="At the archaeologist’s gasp, you learn the truth: the rescue was a trap. They beg you to avenge them and Thorius by killing Lathoric the Black and Obsidion. Curator Thorius in Ironforge needs proof.",h="At the archaeologist’s gasp, you learn the truth: the rescue was a trap.",sec={{t="A Dying Plea",b="The archaeologist can barely speak. They gasp that it was all a trap, ask forgiveness, then plead for you to kill the traitor for them and for Thorius. Lathoric the Black and Obsidion must both fall. Curator Thorius in Ironforge needs proof: one head and one heart.",sp=0},{t="A Voice Answers",b="Dorius calls you fools. He played on his brother’s weak feelings and sent rescuers so they would take the last Suntara stone from the Twilight's Hammer. At the Grimesilt Digsite, he found the Suntara stones. Then Ragnaros's power surged through him and gave him purpose.\n\nBy Ragnaros's will, Obsidion was built to destroy the Blackrock orcs of Blackrock Spire. Reborn as an acolyte of fire, Dorius took the name Lathoric the Black. In Ironforge, Thorius turns pale at the proof: his own brother set all this in motion and betrayed him and Ironforge. Thorius fears the Old Gods still hold strong sway here. If so honorable a man could be turned so easily to Ragnaros, no one is safe.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who gives this quest?",a="A dying archaeologist gives it, begging you to avenge them and Thorius.",al={"quest giver","who starts rise obsidion","dying archaeologist"}},{q="What comes before this quest?",a="Release Them comes before this.",al={"previous quest","prerequisite","chain before rise obsidion"}},{q="Who do you bring the proof to?",a="Bring the proof to Curator Thorius in Ironforge. He wants a head and a heart.",al={"where do i return","who do i return to","where is thorius"}},{q="Who are you sent to slay?",a="You are sent to slay Lathoric the Black and Obsidion.",al={"who is obsidion","who is lathoric","targets"}}},kw={"curator thorius","dying archaeologist","ironforge","lathoric the black","obsidion","ragnaros","rise obsidion","searing gorge"},rel={"quest:3372","zone:searinggorge","zone:ironforge","topic:old-god"},m={start="Dying Archaeologist",["end"]="Curator Thorius",level="46",faction="Alliance",id=3566},src={"Rise, Obsidion!"}}
E["quest:4449"] = {t="quest",n="Caught!",z="searinggorge",s="In Searing Gorge, someone is calling for help from a locked outhouse. The voice inside asks you to teach eight Dark Iron geologists a lesson and bring fifteen pieces of silk cloth, though they offer no reason.",h="In Searing Gorge, someone is calling for help from a locked outhouse.",sec={{t="Locked In",b="The occupant fled the Dark Iron dwarves and hid in the outhouse. They believe the geologists saw them slip inside and used their magic to lock the door before they could get away.",sp=0},{t="Two Favors",b="The trapped person asks you to teach eight Dark Iron geologists a lesson and bring fifteen pieces of silk cloth. When you ask why, they stumble over their words, then say it is for nothing in particular.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is trapped inside the outhouse?",a="An unnamed person who fled the Dark Iron dwarves is trapped inside after hiding in the outhouse.",al={"who is in the outhouse","who is locked in the outhouse","outhouse guy"}},{q="Why does the occupant want silk cloth?",a="The occupant asks for fifteen pieces of silk cloth, then stumbles over the reason and says it is for nothing in particular.",al={"why silk cloth","what is the silk for","why does outhouse guy want silk"}},{q="Who locked the outhouse door?",a="The occupant believes the Dark Iron geologists saw them hide and used their magic to lock the outhouse door.",al={"who locked the door","who trapped the guy","which dark iron dwarves"}},{q="How many geologists must be slain?",a="The occupant asks you to deal with eight Dark Iron geologists.",al={"how many geologists","geologist count"}}},kw={"caught","dark iron geologists","searing gorge","silk cloth","wooden outhouse"},rel={"quest:4450","zone:searinggorge"},m={start="Wooden Outhouse",["end"]="Wooden Outhouse",level="45",id=4449},src={"Caught!"}}
E["quest:4450"] = {t="quest",n="Ledger from Tanaris",z="searinggorge",s="In Searing Gorge, a small job from Tanaris now waits for you. Krinkle Goodsteel of Gadgetzan wants several things gathered here and elsewhere, then brought to him.",h="In Searing Gorge, a small job from Tanaris now waits for you.",sec={{t="A Job from Tanaris",b="The person inside the wooden outhouse has been helped and remembers a small job from Tanaris. Krinkle Goodsteel of Gadgetzan wants several things gathered, some in Searing Gorge and others farther away. The ledger will be slid beneath the door. Carry it and everything listed to Goodsteel in Tanaris.",sp=0},{t="What the Ledger Lists",b="Goodsteel's ledger calls for twenty solid crystal leg shafts from the glassweb spiders of Searing Gorge. It also lists an overdue package at the crashed zeppelin in Beezil's Wreck, in Dustwallow Marsh. The third item is Goodsteel's balanced flameberge. Jarquia, a murloc along the eastern shore of the Swamp of Sorrows, has it.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where does this begin?",a="It begins at the wooden outhouse in Searing Gorge, after you help the person locked inside.",al={"quest start","who gives ledger from tanaris","outhouse location"}},{q="Who is Krinkle Goodsteel?",a="Krinkle Goodsteel is in Gadgetzan, in Tanaris. He says he is awfully busy, with many patrons asking for his services.",al={"who is krinkle goodsteel","krinkle goodsteel gadgetzan","where is krinkle goodsteel"}},{q="What is on the ledger?",a="The ledger lists twenty solid crystal leg shafts, an overdue package, and Goodsteel's balanced flameberge.",al={"what items are needed","ledger item list","goodsteel ledger items"}},{q="Where is the overdue package?",a="The overdue package lies at the crashed zeppelin at Beezil's Wreck, in Dustwallow Marsh.",al={"overdue package location","where is overdue package","beezil's wreck package"}},{q="Who has Goodsteel's balanced flameberge?",a="Jarquia, a murloc along the eastern shore of the Swamp of Sorrows, has Goodsteel's balanced flameberge.",al={"balanced flameberge location","who drops flameberge","jarquia swamp of sorrows"}},{q="What came before this?",a="Caught! came before this, at the same wooden outhouse.",al={"previous quest","prerequisite quest","chain before ledger from tanaris"}}},kw={"beezil's wreck","dustwallow marsh","gadgetzan","glassweb spiders","jarquia","krinkle goodsteel","ledger from tanaris","searing gorge","swamp of sorrows","wooden outhouse"},rel={"quest:4449","subzone:gadgetzan","zone:tanaris","zone:searinggorge","subzone:beezil-s-wreck","zone:dustwallow","zone:swampofsorrows","topic:murloc"},m={start="Wooden Outhouse",["end"]="Krinkle Goodsteel",level="46",id=4450},src={"Ledger from Tanaris"}}
E["quest:4451"] = {t="quest",n="The Key to Freedom",z="searinggorge",s="In Searing Gorge, you have a small brass key with no known destination. Its head reads Dark Iron Outhouse and warns against copying it.",h="In Searing Gorge, you have a small brass key with no known destination.",sec={{t="A Marked Key",b="The small brass key is marked Dark Iron Outhouse, with a warning not to duplicate it. Where it leads remains unknown. Search Searing Gorge for a place that accepts it.",sp=0},{t="An Interrupted Visit",b="A cough comes from inside the wooden outhouse. Someone asks who is there, annoyed at the interruption. Locheed is delighted you found the key. The Dark Irons hid it after locking him inside.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is written on the Grimesilt Outhouse Key?",a="The key's head reads Dark Iron Outhouse and warns against copying it.",al={"key inscription","what does key say","outhouse key text"}},{q="Where does this key lead?",a="You cannot yet tell where the key leads. It is marked for a Dark Iron outhouse, somewhere in Searing Gorge.",al={"where to use key","outhouse location","key to freedom turn in"}}},kw={"dark iron outhouse","grimesilt outhouse key","locheed","searing gorge","the key to freedom","wooden outhouse"},rel={"zone:searinggorge"},m={start="Grimesilt Outhouse Key",["end"]="Wooden Outhouse",level="47",id=4451},src={"The Key to Freedom"}}
E["quest:7701"] = {t="quest",n="WANTED: Overseer Maltorius",z="searinggorge",s="In the Cauldron, a bounty calls for Overseer Maltorius's death. It names him a rogue Thorium Brotherhood agent and the newly hired commander of the Dark Iron Slag Pit crew. Overseer Oilfist orders his head brought to Lookout Captain Lolo Longstriker as proof.",h="In the Cauldron, a bounty calls for Overseer Maltorius's death.",sec={{t="A Price on a Traitor",b="In the Cauldron's Slag Pit, you are sent to find and slay Overseer Maltorius. The notice calls him a traitorous Dark Iron dwarf. Bring his head to Lookout Captain Lolo Longstriker to claim the bounty.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Overseer Maltorius?",a="Overseer Maltorius is a traitorous Dark Iron dwarf. The notice calls him a rogue Thorium Brotherhood agent and the newly hired commander of the Dark Iron Slag Pit crew in the Cauldron.",al={"maltorius lore","who is maltorius","overseer maltorius backstory"}},{q="Where can Overseer Maltorius be found?",a="Overseer Maltorius can be found in the Slag Pit, within the Cauldron.",al={"maltorius location","where is maltorius","how to find overseer maltorius"}},{q="Who ordered the death of Overseer Maltorius?",a="Overseer Oilfist ordered Overseer Maltorius's death.",al={"who posted the bounty","who wants maltorius dead","who ordered the kill"}},{q="Who receives proof of Maltorius's death?",a="Lookout Captain Lolo Longstriker in Searing Gorge receives proof of Maltorius's death: his head.",al={"who to turn in maltorius head","where to bring maltorius head","lolo longstriker location"}}},kw={"bounty","cauldron","lolo longstriker","overseer maltorius","overseer oilfist","searing gorge","slag pit","thorium brotherhood"},rel={"subzone:slag-pit","subzone:cauldron","zone:searinggorge"},m={start="Wanted/Missing/Lost & Found",["end"]="Lookout Captain Lolo Longstriker",level="50",id=7701},src={"WANTED: Overseer Maltorius"}}
E["quest:7704"] = {t="quest",n="Look at the Size of It!",z="searinggorge",s="In the Searing Gorge, you have a gigantic, ornate pillow once kept by Chambermaid Pillaclencher. Evonice Sootsmoker is sure to want it.",h="In the Searing Gorge, you have a gigantic, ornate pillow once kept by Chambermaid Pillaclencher.",sec={{t="A Pillow for Evonice",b="Evonice Sootsmoker is sure to want Chambermaid Pillaclencher's gigantic, ornate pillow. Bring it to her in the Searing Gorge and see what she offers for your trouble.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who wants Chambermaid Pillaclencher's pillow?",a="Evonice Sootsmoker in the Searing Gorge is sure to want Chambermaid Pillaclencher's pillow.",al={"who do i bring the pillow to","evonice sootsmoker pillow","where does the pillow go"}},{q="Where does this pillow come from?",a="The gigantic, ornate pillow once belonged to Chambermaid Pillaclencher.",al={"pillow drop","who drops the pillow","chambermaid pillow"}},{q="Where can Evonice Sootsmoker be found?",a="Evonice Sootsmoker is in the Searing Gorge.",al={"evonice location","where is evonice sootsmoker","evonice searing gorge"}}},kw={"chambermaid pillaclencher","evonice sootsmoker","look at the size of it","pillow","searing gorge"},rel={"zone:searinggorge"},m={start="Chambermaid Pillaclencher's Pillow",level="50",id=7704},src={"Classic quest text: Look at the Size of It!"}}
E["quest:7722"] = {t="quest",n="What the Flux?",z="searinggorge",s="Master Smith Burninate seeks the fiery flux plans in the Slag Pit. Maltorius left their clan with the recipe, which Burninate values above a pristine arcane crystal, and believes the plans are near him.",h="Master Smith Burninate seeks the fiery flux plans in the Slag Pit.",sec={{t="The Stolen Recipe",b="Master Smith Burninate says Maltorius betrayed their clan when he left with the fiery flux recipe. Burninate suspects that recipe helped Maltorius earn his new promotion among the Dark Irons. Now Burninate wants the secret plans returned.",sp=0},{t="Into the Slag Pit",b="Master Smith Burninate believes the plans lie near Maltorius, deep in the Slag Pit. He wants you to carry the Secret Plans: Fiery Flux back to him.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who stole the recipe for fiery flux?",a="Maltorius stole the fiery flux recipe, according to Master Smith Burninate. Burninate calls him a traitor to their clan.",al={"who stole the recipe","who took the plans","what the flux traitor"}},{q="Where are the secret plans?",a="Burninate believes the secret plans lie close to Maltorius, deep in the Cauldron's Slag Pit.",al={"where are the plans","secret plans fiery flux location","where to find fiery flux plans"}},{q="Who asks for the plans to be recovered?",a="Master Smith Burninate, a smith, wants the plans returned.",al={"who gives what the flux","what the flux quest giver"}},{q="Why do the plans matter to Burninate?",a="Burninate says the clan's secret fiery flux recipe is worth more than a pristine arcane crystal.",al={"why is fiery flux important","importance of fiery flux recipe"}}},kw={"burninate","cauldron","fiery flux","maltorius","plans","searing gorge","slag pit"},rel={"zone:searinggorge","subzone:cauldron","subzone:slag-pit","quest:7701"},m={start="Master Smith Burninate",["end"]="Master Smith Burninate",level="50",id=7722},src={"What the Flux?"}}
E["quest:7723"] = {t="quest",n="Curse These Fat Fingers",z="searinggorge",s="In the Searing Gorge, Hansel Heavyhands can no longer deliver beatings as before. Swollen fingers leave Hansel asking you to pound the heavy war golems instead.",h="In the Searing Gorge, Hansel Heavyhands can no longer deliver beatings as before.",sec={{t="Fingers Like Sausages",b="Hansel Heavyhands blames the Searing Gorge climate and its thin air for swelling their fingers. They resemble huge Thelsamar blood sausages. With fingers like these, Hansel can no longer deliver beatings as before, so they need you to handle their business.",sp=0},{t="First on the List",b="Hansel wants you to pound the Gorge's heavy war golems hard. Twenty must be destroyed. They roam the areas around the Cauldron, and you return to Hansel once enough have fallen.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Hansel Heavyhands?",a="Hansel Heavyhands is in the Searing Gorge, where swollen fingers keep them from fighting. Hansel asks you to do the pounding instead.",al={"hansel heavyhands","who gives curse these fat fingers","who is the quest giver"}},{q="Why can Hansel not fight the golems personally?",a="Hansel blames the Searing Gorge climate and thin air for swelling their fingers. They liken them to huge Thelsamar blood sausages.",al={"why are hansels fingers fat","fat fingers lore","hansel swollen hands"}},{q="What foes must be dealt with?",a="You must destroy twenty heavy war golems.",al={"what enemies do i fight","what does hansel want dead"}},{q="Where are the heavy war golems located?",a="The heavy war golems roam the areas around the Cauldron in the Searing Gorge.",al={"where are the golems","heavy war golem location"}}},kw={"cauldron","fat fingers","hansel heavyhands","heavy war golems","searing gorge","thelsamar blood sausages"},rel={"npc:hansel-heavyhands","subzone:cauldron","zone:searinggorge"},m={start="Hansel Heavyhands",["end"]="Hansel Heavyhands",level="49",id=7723},src={"Classic quest text: Curse These Fat Fingers"}}
E["quest:7724"] = {t="quest",n="Fiery Menace!",z="searinggorge",s="Hansel Heavyhands has another job for you in the Searing Gorge. Greater lava spiders are making trouble.",h="Hansel Heavyhands has another job for you in the Searing Gorge.",sec={{t="Another Job for Hansel",b="Hansel Heavyhands has little time to rest or think on his life. Those in power keep giving him more work. Greater lava spiders are causing a ruckus, so Hansel would rather you deal with them.",sp=0},{t="The Greater Lava Spiders",b="Oilfist says the greater lava spiders shoot fire from an awkward place. Their flames upset the children. Hansel wants you to kill twenty spiders on the plateaus and by the lava pools of the Searing Gorge.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who sends you after the spiders?",a="Hansel Heavyhands sends you after the spiders in the Searing Gorge. He had hoped for a quiet moment.",al={"quest giver","who gives quest","hansel"}},{q="Why do the spiders need to be killed?",a="Greater lava spiders are causing a ruckus. Oilfist says the way they shoot fire upsets the children.",al={"why kill spiders","what did spiders do","spider problem"}},{q="Who told Hansel about the spiders?",a="Oilfist told Hansel that the spiders shoot fire from an awkward place.",al={"who complained about spiders","oilfist"}},{q="How many greater lava spiders must be killed?",a="Hansel asks you to kill twenty greater lava spiders.",al={"how many spiders","spider count"}}},kw={"fiery menace","greater lava spiders","hansel heavyhands","oilfist","searing gorge","spiders"},rel={"npc:hansel-heavyhands","zone:searinggorge"},m={start="Hansel Heavyhands",["end"]="Hansel Heavyhands",level="49",id=7724},src={"Fiery Menace!"}}
E["quest:7727"] = {t="quest",n="Incendosaurs? Whateverosaur is More Like It",z="searinggorge",s="Hansel Heavyhands cannot fight with his feet in such disarray. So he sends you to slay twenty incendosaurs in the Slag Pit, where Scrange and Burninate want the lava pools cleared for expeditionary teams.",h="Hansel Heavyhands cannot fight with his feet in such disarray.",sec={{t="Bunions upon Bunions",b="Hansel Heavyhands cannot fight while his bunions are in such a state. Scrange and Burninate told him to kill the incendosaurs so expeditionary teams can explore the Slag Pit’s lava pools. Now he sends you in his place.",sp=0},{t="The Lava Pools",b="The incendosaurs occupy the lava pools in the Slag Pit, within the Cauldron. Hansel wants twenty slain before you return.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Hansel Heavyhands?",a="Hansel Heavyhands gives you work in the Searing Gorge. Scrange and Burninate told him to deal with the incendosaurs, but his bunions keep him from fighting.",al={"hansel heavyhands","who is the quest giver","who gives this quest"}},{q="Why do the incendosaurs need to be cleared out?",a="Scrange and Burninate want expeditionary teams to explore the Slag Pit’s lava pools. The incendosaurs there are said to be causing all kinds of problems.",al={"why kill incendosaurs","incendosaur purpose","why clear the slag pit"}},{q="Where are the incendosaurs found?",a="The incendosaurs live in the lava pools of the Slag Pit, within the Cauldron.",al={"incendosaur location","where is the slag pit","where are the lava pools"}},{q="Why won't Hansel hunt them himself?",a="Hansel says his bunions have bunions. His feet are in too much disarray for him to kill anything.",al={"why won't hansel fight","hansel's feet","hansel bunions"}}},kw={"burninate","cauldron","hansel heavyhands","incendosaur","scrange","searing gorge","slag pit"},rel={"npc:hansel-heavyhands","subzone:slag-pit","subzone:cauldron","zone:searinggorge"},m={start="Hansel Heavyhands",["end"]="Hansel Heavyhands",level="49",faction="Neutral",id=7727},src={"Incendosaurs? Whateverosaur is More Like It"}}
E["quest:7728"] = {t="quest",n="STOLEN: Smithing Tuyere and Lookout's Spyglass",z="searinggorge",s="In the Searing Gorge, the Thorium Brotherhood seeks two stolen tools: a tuyere and a Lookout's Spyglass. The Brotherhood is certain jealous, unscrupulous Dark Iron dwarves took them, and asks that whoever finds them bring them to Taskmaster Scrange for payment.",h="In the Searing Gorge, the Thorium Brotherhood seeks two stolen tools: a tuyere and a Lookout's Spyglass.",sec={{t="Stolen Goods",b="The Thorium Brotherhood seeks a Lookout's Spyglass and a tuyere, both stolen. The spyglass is a fine tool for lookouts, and the tuyere is a smithing tool that cannot be replaced. The Brotherhood is certain Dark Iron dwarves took them. Whoever finds the tools should bring them to Taskmaster Scrange.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who posted the notice?",a="The notice speaks for the Thorium Brotherhood, which is certain Dark Iron dwarves took the items.",al={"who wants the stolen items","who gave this quest","stolen smithing tuyere quest giver"}},{q="Who stole the tools?",a="The Thorium Brotherhood is certain unscrupulous, jealous Dark Iron dwarves of the Searing Gorge stole the tools.",al={"who took the tuyere","who stole the spyglass","who has the stolen items"}},{q="Who receives the recovered items?",a="Taskmaster Scrange receives the recovered items.",al={"where do i turn this in","who is taskmaster scrange","who gets the spyglass"}},{q="What are the stolen items for?",a="The tuyere is an irreplaceable smithing tool, and the spyglass helps lookouts keep watch.",al={"what is a smithing tuyere","why does the brotherhood want the tuyere","what does the spyglass do"}}},kw={"dark iron","scrange","searing gorge","smithing","spyglass","thorium brotherhood","tuyere"},rel={"zone:searinggorge"},m={start="Wanted/Missing/Lost & Found",["end"]="Taskmaster Scrange",level="48",id=7728},src={"STOLEN: Smithing Tuyere and Lookout's Spyglass"}}
E["quest:7729"] = {t="quest",n="JOB OPPORTUNITY: Culling the Competition",z="searinggorge",s="In the Searing Gorge, Taskmaster Scrange wants you to thin the competition through bloody work.",h="In the Searing Gorge, Taskmaster Scrange wants you to thin the competition through bloody work.",sec={{t="An Open Position",b="Taskmaster Scrange sends you through the gorge to kill fifteen Dark Iron Taskmasters and fifteen Dark Iron Slavers. Return when your clothes are bloody enough. You will know when that is, and you are not to ask.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is offering this job?",a="Taskmaster Scrange in the Searing Gorge wants help culling the competition.",al={"who offers this quest","who wants the taskmasters killed","who is taskmaster scrange"}},{q="Which enemies must be slain?",a="Kill fifteen Dark Iron Taskmasters and fifteen Dark Iron Slavers.",al={"what do i kill","targets for job opportunity","who are the competition"}},{q="How does Scrange tell the work is done?",a="Scrange judges by the state of your clothes, weighing you with them and without them to be sure.",al={"how to prove kills","bloody clothes requirement","how does scrange check"}}},kw={"culling the competition","dark iron slaver","dark iron taskmaster","job opportunity","searing gorge","taskmaster scrange"},rel={"zone:searinggorge"},m={start="Wanted/Missing/Lost & Found",["end"]="Taskmaster Scrange",level="48",faction="Neutral",id=7729},src={"JOB OPPORTUNITY: Culling the Competition"}}
E["quest:7736"] = {t="quest",n="Restoring Fiery Flux Supplies via Kingsblood",z="searinggorge",s="In the Searing Gorge, Master Smith Burninate needs more fiery flux after What the Flux?. He asks you for incendosaur scales, Kingsblood, and coal, and accepts all you can offer.",h="In the Searing Gorge, Master Smith Burninate needs more fiery flux after What the Flux?.",sec={{t="Fiery Flux Wanted",b="Master Smith Burninate has little time for talk. His fiery flux is running low, so he asks you for two incendosaur scales, four Kingsblood, and coal. He will take all you can offer.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who asks for these goods?",a="Master Smith Burninate asks for the goods in the Searing Gorge and receives them in person.",al={"who gives this quest","burninate fiery flux","where to turn in"}},{q="What materials does Burninate want?",a="Burninate wants two incendosaur scales, four Kingsblood, and coal.",al={"what items do i need","materials for fiery flux","burninate turn in items"}},{q="What came before this request?",a="What the Flux? came before this request, and Burninate gave it to you.",al={"prereq for this quest","previous quest fiery flux","what the flux prerequisite"}},{q="Why does Burninate want these goods?",a="Burninate says the supply of fiery flux is dwindling and wants it replenished.",al={"why fiery flux","burninate motivation"}}},kw={"burninate","coal","fiery flux","incendosaur","kingsblood","searing gorge","thorium brotherhood"},rel={"quest:7722","zone:searinggorge"},m={start="Master Smith Burninate",["end"]="Master Smith Burninate",level="60",id=7736},src={"Restoring Fiery Flux Supplies via Kingsblood"}}
E["quest:8241"] = {t="quest",n="Restoring Fiery Flux Supplies via Iron",z="searinggorge",s="In the Searing Gorge, fiery flux is running low, and Master Smith Burninate needs more. After What the Flux?, Burninate asks for scales, iron bars, and coal, and will take all you can offer.",h="In the Searing Gorge, fiery flux is running low, and Master Smith Burninate needs more.",sec={{t="Fiery Flux Wanted",b="Master Smith Burninate needs more fiery flux as the supply runs low. In the Searing Gorge, Burninate asks you for two incendosaur scales, four iron bars, and coal. All you can offer will be taken.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who asks for these goods?",a="Master Smith Burninate asks for the goods and receives them in person in the Searing Gorge.",al={"who gives this quest","burninate fiery flux","where to turn in"}},{q="What materials does Burninate want?",a="Burninate wants two incendosaur scales, four iron bars, and coal.",al={"what items do i need","materials for fiery flux","burninate turn in items"}},{q="What came before this request?",a="What the Flux? came before this request, and Burninate gave it to you.",al={"prereq for this quest","previous quest fiery flux","what the flux prerequisite"}},{q="Why does Burninate want these goods?",a="Burninate says the supply of fiery flux is dwindling, so more is needed to replenish it.",al={"why fiery flux","burninate motivation"}}},kw={"coal","fiery flux","incendosaur scale","iron bar","master smith burninate","restoring fiery flux supplies via iron","searing gorge","thorium brotherhood"},rel={"quest:7722","zone:searinggorge"},m={start="Master Smith Burninate",["end"]="Master Smith Burninate",level="60",id=8241},src={"Restoring Fiery Flux Supplies via Iron"}}
E["quest:8242"] = {t="quest",n="Restoring Fiery Flux Supplies via Heavy Leather",z="searinggorge",s="In the Searing Gorge, Master Smith Burninate needs more fiery flux supplies. After What the Flux?, he asks you for two incendosaur scales, ten pieces of heavy leather, and coal. Bring all you can offer.",h="In the Searing Gorge, Master Smith Burninate needs more fiery flux supplies.",sec={{t="Fiery Flux Wanted",b="Master Smith Burninate needs more fiery flux in the Searing Gorge. The supply is running low, so he asks you for two incendosaur scales, ten pieces of heavy leather, and coal. Bring all you can offer.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who asks for these goods?",a="Master Smith Burninate asks for the goods in the Searing Gorge and receives them in person.",al={"who gives this quest","burninate fiery flux","where to turn in"}},{q="What materials does Burninate want?",a="Burninate wants two incendosaur scales, ten pieces of heavy leather, and coal.",al={"what items do i need","materials for fiery flux","burninate turn in items"}},{q="What came before this request?",a="Before this request, Burninate gave you What the Flux?.",al={"prereq for this quest","previous quest fiery flux","what the flux prerequisite"}},{q="Why does Burninate want these goods?",a="Burninate says the fiery flux supply is running low and needs replenishing.",al={"why fiery flux","burninate motivation"}}},kw={"burninate","coal","fiery flux","heavy leather","incendosaur scale","searing gorge","thorium brotherhood"},rel={"quest:7722","zone:searinggorge"},m={start="Master Smith Burninate",["end"]="Master Smith Burninate",level="60",id=8242},src={"Restoring Fiery Flux Supplies via Heavy Leather"}}
E["subzone:blackchar-cave"] = {t="subzone",n="Blackchar Cave",z="searinggorge",s="In southwestern Searing Gorge, rubble seals Blackchar Cave against the crags.",h="In southwestern Searing Gorge, rubble seals Blackchar Cave against the crags.",sec={{t="A Sealed Threshold",b="Blackchar Cave sits among the crags near the approach to Blackrock Mountain. Rubble and scorched slag seal its entrance, closing every tunnel beyond. Ash and magma scar the barren ground around it.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Can you go inside Blackchar Cave?",a="No. Collapsed rock, ash, and rubble seal Blackchar Cave’s entrance, leaving no open interior to explore.",al={"is blackchar cave open","enter blackchar cave","inside blackchar cave"}},{q="Where is Blackchar Cave located?",a="Blackchar Cave lies in southwestern Searing Gorge, among rocky foothills near the passage toward Blackrock Mountain.",al={"blackchar cave location","where is blackchar cave"}}},kw={"blackchar cave","blackrock mountain","sealed cave","searing gorge"},rel={"zone:searinggorge","subzone:blackrock-mountain"},src={"Blackchar Cave"}}
E["subzone:cauldron"] = {t="subzone",n="Cauldron",z="searinggorge",s="In the Searing Gorge, Dark Iron miners drive their work at Cauldron under the watch of overseers and fire elementals. Captured slaves labor in its depths, where heat and torment have driven many mad.",h="In the Searing Gorge, Dark Iron miners drive their work at Cauldron under the watch of overseers and fire...",sec={{t="The Molten Quarry",b="At the center of the Searing Gorge, Cauldron cuts deep into scorched earth. The Dark Irons fortified the pit after Emperor Thaurissan summoned Ragnaros with catastrophic results. Heavy excavation machines scrape rock and ore from the smoldering stone along the canyon walls. Below, fire and magma elementals prowl beside Dark Iron taskmasters. Heat rises from the mountain's depths.",sp=0},{t="The Broken Workforce",b="Captured slaves endure brutal shifts beneath the lash of Dark Iron overseers. Relentless labor, sweltering heat, and torment have driven many mad. They can no longer tell friend from foe. Anyone who disturbs their work is struck, even those who might offer a chance at freedom.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Cauldron?",a="Cauldron is a vast open-pit mine at the center of the Searing Gorge. The Dark Iron clan fortified it to extract stone and ore amid intense volcanic heat.",al={"the cauldron lore","what is the cauldron","searing gorge quarry"}},{q="Who controls the excavation?",a="The Dark Iron clan commands the excavation with heavy machinery and armed overseers. They rule the pit and its laborers.",al={"who runs the cauldron","cauldron masters"}},{q="Why do the slaves attack adventurers who try to help?",a="Cruel torment, blinding heat, and endless exhaustion have driven the slaves mad. They see anyone interrupting their work as a threat and attack those nearby.",al={"why are slaves hostile","slave workers attacking","can you free the slaves"}},{q="What kinds of creatures live inside the pit?",a="Dark Iron overseers and enslaved workers occupy the pit. Fire and magma elementals prowl its fiery fissures.",al={"cauldron mobs","what is in the cauldron","monsters in cauldron"}}},ang={["profession:Mining"]="Cauldron's heavy machines and open terraces reveal the scale of Dark Iron mining, cut into unstable volcanic crust.",["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf of Ironforge, seeing the Dark Irons use captured people as broken labor among fire elementals stirs deep disgust."},kw={"cauldron","dark iron","excavation","magma elementals","quarry","searing gorge","slave workers","slaves"},rel={"zone:searinggorge","topic:dark-iron-clan","subzone:ruins-of-thaurissan"},src={"Cauldron"}}
E["subzone:dustfire-valley"] = {t="subzone",n="Dustfire Valley",z="searinggorge",s="At Searing Gorge’s northern edge, Dustfire Valley ends at the locked gate of Stonewrought Pass and the road to Loch Modan.",h="At Searing Gorge’s northern edge, Dustfire Valley ends at the locked gate of Stonewrought Pass and the road...",sec={{t="The Northern Boundary",b="Ash lies across the rock in Dustfire Valley, where bare canyon walls rise around you. At its northern end, a locked dwarven gate seals Stonewrought Pass. The doors bar direct travel to the Valley of Kings and Loch Modan, leaving the valley a dead end amid Searing Gorge’s sulfurous wastes.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where does the gate in Dustfire Valley lead?",a="The gate seals Stonewrought Pass, a mountain passage through the heights to the Valley of Kings in Loch Modan.",al={"dustfire gate","locked door dustfire","where does stonewrought pass lead"}},{q="Can you open the gate to Loch Modan?",a="The dwarven gate is locked to protect Loch Modan from threats in Searing Gorge. A specific key is needed to pass through.",al={"how to open gate","open stonewrought pass","key to dustfire gate"}},{q="Why is this area called Dustfire Valley?",a="Dustfire Valley takes its name from the volcanic ash, dry dust, and lingering heat in the canyon near the northern mountain walls.",al={"dustfire valley name","why dustfire"}}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you know this heavily fortified gate marks a back door between the safety of Khaz Modan and territory ruled by the Dark Iron clan."},kw={"dustfire valley","loch modan","locked gate","searing gorge","stonewrought pass","valley of kings"},rel={"subzone:stonewrought-pass","subzone:valley-of-kings","zone:searinggorge","zone:lochmodan"},src={"Dustfire Valley"}}
E["subzone:firewatch-ridge"] = {t="subzone",n="Firewatch Ridge",z="searinggorge",s="Dark Iron dwarves hold Firewatch Ridge above the Cauldron in northern Searing Gorge. Their sentries, golems, and fire spiders guard the bluff, while the Twilight's Hammer holds caves to the northwest.",h="Dark Iron dwarves hold Firewatch Ridge above the Cauldron in northern Searing Gorge.",sec={{t="A Scorched Vantage Point",b="From Firewatch Ridge, you look down on the Cauldron's industrial devastation. Dark Iron guards, engineers, and molten golems patrol the crags, defending their foothold beside venomous flame spiders native to the smoldering rocks. The height lets the Dark Irons watch the ash plains and spot incursions from Ironforge or the Thorium Brotherhood early.",sp=0},{t="The Shadow of the Cult",b="The Twilight's Hammer holds a cave network in the ridge's northwestern reaches. Its cultists work in the Dark Iron camp's shadow, performing dark rituals below the rock, where powerful elite zealots keep watch. The caves lie near both the Dark Iron works and Blackrock Mountain. Elemental and apocalyptic cults meet in Searing Gorge's fiery heart.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Firewatch Ridge?",a="Firewatch Ridge rises above the Cauldron excavation in Searing Gorge, where the Dark Iron dwarves keep a major camp.",al={"what is this place","firewatch ridge info","firewatch ridge overview"}},{q="What enemies inhabit Firewatch Ridge?",a="Hostile Dark Iron dwarves, mechanical golems, and native fire spiders inhabit the ridge. Elite Twilight's Hammer cultists hold the cave network to the northwest.",al={"what mobs are here","enemies firewatch","firewatch ridge threats"}},{q="Why is the Twilight's Hammer here?",a="The Twilight's Hammer occupies the ridge's northwestern caves to pursue elemental worship and apocalyptic rituals near Blackrock Mountain and the fire elementals bound in the region.",al={"twilights hammer firewatch","cultists in cave","northwest cave firewatch"}},{q="How does Firewatch Ridge relate to the Cauldron?",a="Firewatch Ridge rises directly above the Cauldron, giving the Dark Iron dwarves a fortified vantage point to oversee mining and defend their quarry from attack.",al={"firewatch and cauldron","cauldron overlook","why overlook cauldron"}}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf of Ironforge, you can see Firewatch Ridge as a grim reminder of your Dark Iron cousins' entrenched malice, iron industry, and dark alliances beneath Blackrock Mountain."},kw={"cauldron","dark iron","firewatch ridge","flame spiders","golems","searing gorge","twilight's hammer"},rel={"subzone:cauldron","zone:searinggorge","topic:twilight-s-hammer"},src={"Firewatch Ridge"}}
E["subzone:grimesilt-dig-site"] = {t="subzone",n="Grimesilt Dig Site",z="searinggorge",s="Dark Iron sentries patrol the Grimesilt Dig Site in the Searing Gorge. Ironforge's search for relics began here, and its surviving crew struggles to endure in hiding.",h="Dark Iron sentries patrol the Grimesilt Dig Site in the Searing Gorge.",sec={{t="A Contested Excavation",b="Dark Iron sentries patrol the Grimesilt Dig Site in the Searing Gorge. Ironforge scholars first sent an expedition beneath the crags to seek relics. The native Dark Iron dwarves drove the excavators out and seized their equipment. Wounded and scattered, the original crew remains trapped in and around the pit.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who originally established the Grimesilt Dig Site?",a="Bronzebeard dwarves of Ironforge began the excavation. Their team came to unearth ancient artifacts beneath the Searing Gorge, but the Dark Iron dwarves ambushed them and drove them away.",al={"who dug grimesilt","who made grimesilt dig site","grimesilt founders"}},{q="Who controls the dig site now?",a="The Dark Iron clan controls the excavation. They occupy the pits and guard the remaining tools and territory against any Ironforge attempt to reclaim the area.",al={"who owns grimesilt","grimesilt enemies","who is at grimesilt"}},{q="Are there any survivors from the original crew?",a="Yes. A few workers survived, including the injured excavator Dorius Stonetender, who lies near the pit floor. Another crewmate hides inside a nearby outhouse.",al={"survivors at grimesilt","dorius stonetender","who is trapped at grimesilt"}}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="For Bronzebeard dwarves, Grimesilt is a bitter reminder of the Dark Iron threat across the mountains and the dangers dwarven antiquities and archaeologists face in hostile lands.",["faction:Alliance"]="The dig site marks an Ironforge endeavor broken by the Dark Irons. Beleaguered Alliance subjects wait for extraction in treacherous territory."},kw={"archaeology","dark iron","dorius stonetender","excavation","grimesilt dig site","ironforge","searing gorge"},rel={"zone:searinggorge","zone:ironforge","topic:dwarf"},src={"Grimesilt Dig Site"}}
E["subzone:sea-of-cinders"] = {t="subzone",n="Sea of Cinders",z="searinggorge",s="Ash and embers sweep the Sea of Cinders, north of Blackrock Mountain.",h="Ash and embers sweep the Sea of Cinders, north of Blackrock Mountain.",sec={{t="A Wasteland of Embers",b="Ash and burning grit sweep the plain between the Searing Gorge cliffs and Blackrock Mountain. Centuries ago, the Firelord Ragnaros was summoned into the mortal world. The upheaval fractured the Redridge Mountains and left the surrounding land an arid slag heap. The Sea of Cinders is one of the cataclysm’s most barren remnants, where the earth never cools.",sp=0},{t="Peril Beneath the Slopes",b="Travelers and scavengers taking the north approach to Blackrock Mountain often cross these scorching flats. Winds drive blinding ash clouds across the way, hiding sudden fissures, elemental horrors, and predators adapted to the heat. Dark Iron dwarves claim this hostile land. Anyone crossing the cinders must stay watchful and move swiftly.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Sea of Cinders?",a="The Sea of Cinders lies in southern Searing Gorge, against the northern face of Blackrock Mountain. Smoldering dirt and flying embers blanket this desolate flatland.",al={"what is sea of cinders","sea of cinders lore","where is sea of cinders"}},{q="Why is the ground constantly burning?",a="Centuries ago, Sorcerer-Thane Thaurissan summoned the Firelord Ragnaros during the War of the Three Hammers. The eruption superheated the earth and shattered the mountains, and the plains still smolder.",al={"why is it on fire","why are there cinders","why does the ground smoke"}},{q="Does anyone live here?",a="No organized settlement stands within the Sea of Cinders. Heat, poor air, and lack of water make permanent habitation impossible, though wandering beasts, fire elementals, and patrols affiliated with Blackrock Mountain cross the expanse.",al={"who lives here","sea of cinders inhabitants","settlements"}},{q="What makes traveling through here dangerous?",a="Hostile beasts and Dark Iron dwarves threaten travelers near the mountain. Blinding soot and burning ash fill the air, while deep thermal rifts split the flat terrain.",al={"is it safe","dangers of sea of cinders"}}},ang={["profession:Mining"]="Heat-cracked stone near Blackrock Mountain can expose rich mineral deposits and dark iron veins to those who brave the drifting ash.",["race:Dwarf"]="As a Bronzebeard or Wildhammer dwarf, you walk through wastes that recall Thaurissan's folly and the dark powers that shattered the Redridge Mountains."},kw={"ash","blackrock mountain","dark iron","embers","ragnaros","sea of cinders","searing gorge","wasteland"},rel={"zone:searinggorge","subzone:blackrock-mountain"},src={"Sea of Cinders"}}
E["subzone:slag-pit"] = {t="subzone",n="Slag Pit",z="searinggorge",s="In the Cauldron, the Slag Pit drives the Dark Iron dwarves’ mining. Slavers force workers through the tunnels while incendosaurs prowl below.",h="In the Cauldron, the Slag Pit drives the Dark Iron dwarves’ mining.",sec={{t="Subterranean Toil",b="The Slag Pit cuts into the Cauldron, where Dark Iron dwarves force enslaved workers to mine ore and minerals. Overseers and taskmasters keep them digging day and night. Beneath Blackrock Mountain, the tunnels feed supply lines to Blackrock Depths. The Dark Irons guard those lines against anyone who interferes.",sp=0},{t="Depths of the Pit",b="Below, the tunnels open into scorching caverns where incendosaurs roam. These fierce reptiles threaten workers and intruders alike. Still, the Dark Iron masters drive their laborers deeper into the rock, heedless of the lives lost.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is the Slag Pit located?",a="The Slag Pit lies deep inside the Cauldron, the great excavation crater at the center of Searing Gorge. Its tunnels run beneath the surface mining works.",al={"slag pit location","where is slag pit","how to get to slag pit"}},{q="Who controls the Slag Pit?",a="Dark Iron slavers and taskmasters control the Slag Pit. They patrol its shafts and drive their captives to dig around the clock.",al={"who runs slag pit","slag pit faction","dark irons slag pit"}},{q="Why do the slave workers attack intruders?",a="Enslaved workers are not hostile on their own, but fear of their Dark Iron masters runs deep. When a nearby slaver or taskmaster is attacked, the laborers rush to defend the overseer to avoid punishment.",al={"why do slaves attack","hostile slaves","slave workers aggro"}},{q="What creatures live in the Slag Pit?",a="Dark Iron dwarves, enslaved workers, and incendosaurs live in the Slag Pit. The incendosaurs prowl its deepest tunnels.",al={"monsters in slag pit","incendosaurs","slag pit beasts"}}},ang={["profession:Mining"]="The Slag Pit’s deep shafts cut into Searing Gorge’s mineral-rich rock, where rich ore waits at great danger.",["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf of Ironforge, you see the bitter divide between the clans in the cruelty of the Dark Iron slavers."},kw={"cauldron","dark iron","incendosaur","searing gorge","slag pit","slaver","slaves","taskmaster"},rel={"subzone:cauldron","zone:searinggorge"},src={"Slag Pit"}}
E["subzone:stonewrought-pass"] = {t="subzone",n="Stonewrought Pass",z="searinggorge",s="Iron gates bar Stonewrought Pass between Loch Modan and Searing Gorge. Franclorn Forgewright cut the tunnel through the southern mountains, joining the Valley of Kings to Dustfire Valley and shielding dwarven lands from the volcanic dangers beyond.",h="Iron gates bar Stonewrought Pass between Loch Modan and Searing Gorge.",sec={{t="A Gateway Carved in Stone",b="Franclorn Forgewright carved Stonewrought Pass through the bedrock. The master architect also built the massive Stonewrought Dam. The tunnel runs from Loch Modan near the Valley of Kings, through the mountain ridge, and down into Dustfire Valley. Dark Iron dwarves and fiery beasts threaten travelers in Searing Gorge. So the Ironforge mountaineers keep heavy gates locked at both ends, guarding the way north into Loch Modan.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where does the Stonewrought Pass lead?",a="Stonewrought Pass runs through the mountains from the Valley of Kings on Loch Modan’s southern edge to Dustfire Valley in northern Searing Gorge.",al={"where does stonewrought pass go","tunnel connection","searing gorge to loch modan"}},{q="Who designed this tunnel?",a="Franclorn Forgewright, the master dwarven architect, designed the tunnel. Across Khaz Modan, he is famed for the Stonewrought Dam and other monumental stone works.",al={"who built stonewrought pass","architect of pass","franclorn forgewright tunnel"}},{q="Why are the gates locked?",a="Heavy gates bar the pass against Searing Gorge’s fiery monsters and hostile Dark Iron dwarves. Mountaineer Pebblebitty guards the Loch Modan entrance and requires authorization before allowing passage.",al={"locked gate","why is pass locked","how to open gate"}}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you can see Franclorn Forgewright’s skill in the tunnel’s stonework. The pass now borders territory conquered by your wayward Dark Iron kin.",["faction:Alliance"]="Dwarven Mountaineers guard this locked passage, shielding Loch Modan’s vulnerable settlements from the volcanic threats in Searing Gorge."},kw={"dustfire valley","franclorn forgewright","loch modan","pebblebitty","searing gorge","stonewrought pass","valley of kings"},rel={"subzone:dustfire-valley","subzone:valley-of-kings","zone:searinggorge","zone:lochmodan","subzone:stonewrought-dam","topic:alliance"},src={"Stonewrought Pass"}}
E["subzone:thorium-point"] = {t="subzone",n="Thorium Point",z="searinggorge",s="At Thorium Point, the Thorium Brotherhood holds its ground against Dark Iron kin who serve the Firelord and Emperor Dagran Thaurissan. The outpost welcomes Alliance and Horde travelers who will gather ore or fight in the volcanic wastes.",h="At Thorium Point, the Thorium Brotherhood holds its ground against Dark Iron kin who serve the Firelord and...",sec={{t="A Foothold Above the Ash",b="Thorium Point clings to the northern bluffs above the scorched slag heaps of the Searing Gorge. The Thorium Brotherhood holds this mountain camp. Its Dark Iron dwarves broke from their enslaved kin in Shadowforge City and refuse to bow to the Firelord or Emperor Dagran Thaurissan.\n\nAn open-air forge, a busy flight master, and guarded walls give the Brotherhood a foothold northeast of Firewatch Ridge. They struggle to survive and seek mastery of smithing. With few allies, they open the camp to both Alliance and Horde travelers, who can dig ore from the ash or fight the Dark Iron dwarves.",sp=0},{t="A Waystation for Wayfarers",b="Thorium Point gives the Brotherhood a base for war against its kin and a safe crossing through the Redridge mountain chain. The camp overlooks a volcanic basin where ravenous spiders and fire elementals prowl.\n\nFlight links reach Ironforge and forward camps across the Badlands and the Burning Steppes. Mercenaries, prospectors, and crafters seeking the secret favor of master dwarf smiths find a safe hearth on this smoky cliffside.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who controls Thorium Point?",a="The Thorium Brotherhood controls Thorium Point. Its Dark Iron dwarves broke away from their fiery emperor and seek to live free of elemental servitude.",al={"who runs thorium point","thorium point owner","who lives at thorium point"}},{q="Why is Thorium Point neutral to both the Alliance and Horde?",a="The Thorium Brotherhood faces more hostile Dark Iron kin and beasts than it can fight alone. It trades freely and hires adventurers from either faction because it cannot afford more enemies.",al={"why can horde use thorium point","is thorium point neutral","alliance horde thorium point"}},{q="What services are available at Thorium Point?",a="Thorium Point has flight masters with links to Ironforge, the Badlands, and the Burning Steppes. Trade vendors, a working forge and anvil, and local work against the Dark Iron dwarves are also available.",al={"flight path thorium point","what is at thorium point","thorium point vendors"}},{q="Where is Thorium Point located in Searing Gorge?",a="Thorium Point lies high along Searing Gorge's northern rock wall, northeast of Firewatch Ridge, overlooking the caldera floor.",al={"how to find thorium point","thorium point location","where is thorium point"}}},ang={["profession:Blacksmithing"]="Dark Iron smiths at Thorium Point keep trade secrets coveted by metalworkers across the world. They offer rare plans to crafters who bring volcanic ore and components.",["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you may rarely meet Dark Iron dwarves who do not try to kill you. Bronzebeard travelers know these outcasts are driven by craft and survival, not love for Ironforge."},kw={"blacksmithing","dark iron","firewatch ridge","flight path","searing gorge","thorium brotherhood","thorium point"},rel={"zone:searinggorge","subzone:firewatch-ridge","zone:burningsteppes","subzone:flame-crest","subzone:morgan-s-vigil","zone:ironforge","zone:badlands","subzone:kargath"},src={"Thorium Point"}}
E["zone:searinggorge"] = {t="zone",n="Searing Gorge",z="searinggorge",s="In Searing Gorge, the Dark Iron clan works a land once joined to the green Redridge Mountains. Ragnaros the Firelord scorched it when he was summoned over two centuries ago. Now the Thorium Brotherhood watches the clan's slave mines in the Cauldron.",h="In Searing Gorge, the Dark Iron clan works a land once joined to the green Redridge Mountains.",sec={{t="A Scorched Wasteland",b="Before the War of the Three Hammers, Searing Gorge was a green, rolling part of the Redridge chain. That land was lost over two hundred and thirty years ago. Sorcerer-Thane Thaurissan summoned Ragnaros from deep beneath the world, hoping to turn defeat into victory. The Firelord tore the earth apart, raised Blackrock Mountain and reduced the great Dark Iron city of Thaurissan to smoking ruins. Ash, sulfur and volcanic glass covered the northern valley.",sp=0},{t="The Cauldron and the Slag Pit",b="After their old capital fell, the Dark Iron dwarves seized the gorge for the materials their war machine needed. At the valley's heart, the Cauldron cuts deep into the stone as a vast open-pit excavation. In its lower reaches, the Slag Pit forms a harsh underground mining complex.\n\nDark Iron overseers and lumbering war golems force captured enemies into slave labor, hauling iron, mithril and rare Dark Iron ore from burning rock. Lava surges and roaming beasts threaten the miners at every turn.",sp=0},{t="Thorium Brotherhood and Contested Paths",b="Thorium Point crowns the northern crags above the excavation. The Thorium Brotherhood holds this fortified outpost, after splitting from its kin in Blackrock Mountain. Its master craftsmen offer travelers neutral shelter in return for undermining Dark Iron operations or bringing rare smelting components.\n\nAccess to the gorge remains tightly controlled. The Alliance bars Stonewrought Pass toward Loch Modan with heavy iron gates, while Horde expeditions from nearby Kargath have cut a narrow trail through the eastern badlands to scout the region.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is the Searing Gorge burned and covered in ash?",a="Over two hundred and thirty years ago, during the War of the Three Hammers, the Dark Iron Sorcerer-Thane Thaurissan tried to summon a supernatural power to escape defeat. Instead, he brought forth Ragnaros the Firelord. The eruption shattered the southern Redridge range, raised Blackrock Mountain and burned the surrounding valleys into Searing Gorge and the Burning Steppes.",al={"why is it burnt","searing gorge lore","how was searing gorge created"}},{q="Who are the dwarves living at Thorium Point?",a="The dwarves at Thorium Point belong to the Thorium Brotherhood, an independent faction of Dark Iron dwarves who broke ties with their imperial kin beneath Blackrock Mountain. From their camp atop Thorium Point, they work as master smiths and artificers. They trade knowledge and crafting secrets with travelers who aid them against the Dark Iron forces below.",al={"thorium point dwarves","who is thorium brotherhood","thorium brotherhood lore"}},{q="What is going on in the Cauldron?",a="The Dark Iron clan controls the Cauldron, a vast open excavation that holds the underground Slag Pit. Overseers and war golems force captured prisoners into slave labor, mining precious ores, including Dark Iron, for the great forges inside Blackrock Mountain.",al={"what is the cauldron","the slag pit lore","what are dark irons mining"}},{q="How do you get into Searing Gorge from Loch Modan?",a="Stonewrought Pass from Loch Modan is barred by a heavy locked gate guarded by Ironforge mountaineers. You can obtain the Key to Searing Gorge through an official task for Curator Thorius, ask a skilled rogue to pick the lock, or bypass the gate by taking the open trail south of Kargath in the Badlands.",al={"stonewrought pass gate","how to open searing gorge door","key to searing gorge"}},{q="Why is the Horde interested in Searing Gorge?",a="The Horde uses nearby Kargath in the Badlands as a base. Its commanders cut a mountain pass into the gorge to scout Dark Iron troop movements and secure routes toward Blackrock Mountain, a place of great strategic importance.",al={"why is horde here","kargath gorge connection","horde presence"}},{q="Are there any dungeons or raid entrances inside Searing Gorge?",a="No instance portals open directly inside Searing Gorge, but its southern entrance leads into Blackrock Mountain. The mountain holds Blackrock Depths, Blackrock Spire and the deep passages to the Molten Core.",al={"searing gorge instances","dungeons in searing gorge","where is molten core"}}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf of Ironforge, you can see Searing Gorge as a bitter reminder of the War of the Three Hammers and the Dark Iron clan's disastrous folly. Their excavations now threaten Khaz Modan's southern approaches.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler, you find Stonewrought Pass barred to keep the Dark Irons apart from peaceful dwarven settlements in Loch Modan. The Alliance sanctions courageous adventurers to strike into the gorge.",["faction:Horde"]="As a Horde traveler, you can use Kargath as a staging base. The Horde cut an overland route into the gorge to gather intelligence on Blackrock Mountain and disrupt Dark Iron operations in Khaz Modan.",["profession:Mining"]="As a miner, you can seek rich veins of mithril, truesilver and coveted Dark Iron ore in the volcanic wastes and the deep Slag Pit excavations.",["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, your seasoned lockpicking can open the Stonewrought Pass gate between Loch Modan and the gorge."},kw={"blackrock mountain","cauldron","dark iron clan","ragnaros","searing gorge","slag pit","stonewrought pass","thorium brotherhood","thorium point"},rel={"subzone:blackrock-mountain","subzone:thorium-point","subzone:cauldron","subzone:slag-pit","subzone:stonewrought-pass","zone:badlands","zone:burningsteppes","topic:dark-iron-clan"},src={"Searing Gorge (Classic)","Searing Gorge"}}
